id: pm-vcs-phase6moves
title: Preserve explicit FileId intent for ambiguous edited moves
description: "Same-inode rename plus edit and unambiguous unchanged-content moves retain FileIds today. An edited move across filesystems can lose both inode and content evidence, so guessing can conflate independent files. Add an explicit native move or identity-mapping operation with collision and erasure guards."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-vcs#189"
created_at: "2026-10-21T15:48:35.100Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-06T23:54:31.835Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: An explicitly declared edited move retains its FileId and PM ChangeId trace across filesystems; independent copies keep new identities; ambiguous inference never silently picks an unrelated source.
parent: pm-vcs-b7cb
comments[21]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T18:11:18.317Z",codex-astra,"Design: add explicit FileId mapping to native staging, validated under the shared writer lease and committed in the existing index/tree identity fields. Reserve declared identities before inference; return typed ambiguous_move with candidate paths and a concrete remedy for tied move evidence. Align three-way merge inputs by unique FileId before content merging so replay uses the same path. Tests will cover adversarial pairing, seeded oracle sequences, separate processes, and crash/retry/clone convergence. Full release certification remains in CI as requested."
  "2026-11-06T18:19:42.161Z",codex-astra,Implementation uses the existing tree FileId as durable move authority. Focused attribution tests pass 7/7. The seeded identity-keyed oracle passed 18 rounds of two-sided edits/moves plus reversed merges; separate-process disjoint and competing declarations passed. Merge and rebase produced the same tree; fatal before/after-index cuts recovered and cloned correctly. Working stat hints are intentionally excluded from byte-equality claims; canonical committed tree/payload bytes are checked.
  "2026-11-06T18:25:27.816Z",codex-astra,"Behavioral revert proofs in a disposable source copy: reverting only Repository.stage/stageLocked to main made all 7 selected tests fail (explicit authority, ambiguous candidates, invalid intent corpus, OS-process claims, both SIGKILL boundaries, real PM command). Restoring staging and reverting only mergeTrees made both the merge/rebase/clone regression and seeded oracle fail (2/2). The unchanged implementation passes the 10-test suite, and c8 reports 100/100/100/100 on engine/moves.ts and engine/merge-moves.ts. Additional guard fixtures and broader existing regressions are running before final certification."
  "2026-11-06T18:33:28.051Z",codex-astra,"Local validation complete: new regression suite 12/12 through pinned pm test --run --only-index 1 --progress --timeout 600; broader staging, attribution, model, repository, rewrite and command regressions 158/158, no skips or cancellations. All 12 new tests fail on behavioral reverts in disposable copies: stage/stageLocked 7/7 plus the two additional guard tests 2/2; mergeTrees 2/2; alignFileMoves 1/1. Restored code passes. New modules have measured 100/100/100/100 coverage. Build, test typecheck, lint, docstrings, zero-duplication and production audit pass. Full npm and Bun release gates remain assigned to CI. The tracker disables test-result persistence, so the exact run receipt is summarized here without changing policy. CLI UX observation: invalid files/docs argument usage returned a zero shell exit despite reporting an error; corrected repeated --add forms succeeded."
  "2026-11-06T18:39:13.592Z",codex-astra,Committed self-host verification passed at 243c627 after post-commit regeneration (no archive change). Package privacy passed for 365 files with zero findings; release changelog-date and publish-attestation checks passed. The all-object identity audit refuses one address in the shared physical database; a fresh reachable-only clone of this exact candidate passes with five approved identities. Existing pm-vcs-identity-isolation tracks the unrelated shared-object limitation. No audit weakening or history rewrite was performed.
  "2026-11-06T18:44:12.599Z",codex-astra,"Opened PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/189 at 478e3e4 and immediately queued CodeRabbit round 1. GraphQL rate limiting prevented gh pr create; a REST read proved no existing PR before one REST creation. Exact-head CI is queued at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/42273246563 and CodeQL at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/42273246633. The final candidate also passed the unchanged all-object audit in a fresh reachable-only clone. Review and CI are pending evidence, not approval."
  "2026-11-06T18:54:56.748Z",codex-astra,"Self-review found and fixed a scale regression in the new plan-before-publish staging flow: retained small-file snapshots are now capped at four MiB. Excess snapshots are released and reread with the same canonical hash function and mode checks before publication. A separate-process fixture stages 32 half-MiB files and checks live ArrayBuffer growth plus real content/mode drift refusals. The bounded implementation passes; restoring only stage/stageLocked from the first PR head makes this new test fail with 16,318,468 bytes retained above baseline against a six-MiB allowance. CodeRabbit automatic review was skipped; the requested manual queue remains pending. Greptile reported an expired trial and Sourcery exhausted its budget; these are missing reviews, not approval."
  "2026-11-06T18:57:09.120Z",codex-astra,"Final implementation validation: the expanded regression suite passes 13/13 through pinned pm test (no skips or cancellations); seven focused cache, streaming, symlink, record and link regressions pass after bounded rereads. The two new modules remain measured at 100/100/100/100, and the shared canonical staging hash helper is exercised for blob, record and link payloads. The additional memory/drift regression fails on the unbounded staging-function revert; all 13 tests now have behavioral revert evidence. Releasing my claim for review and orchestrator verification; the item stays in_progress and is not closed. Full CI and the queued review remain pending, with final exact-head receipts to be reported on PR 189."
  "2026-11-06T21:48:48.547Z",codex-astra,"CI on 35f9df3: Node 26 completed the full npm gate and is running Bun. Node 22 ran 2646 tests: 2645 passed and the new memory fixture failed (11,021,198 bytes against its six-MiB allowance); coverage also reported gaps on that runtime. Reclaiming the item to reproduce the runtime-specific measurement and fix the gate without lowering production thresholds. CodeRabbit is processing the queued final-head review."
  "2026-11-06T21:53:22.127Z",codex-astra,"CI failure diagnosis: the new memory child omitted the existing release-suite --no-concurrent-array-buffer-sweeping flag, so Node 22 could count unreachable backing stores after explicit GC. Added that same child flag; production code, memory allowance and all coverage thresholds are unchanged. Fixed suite passes 13/13 on Node 22.23.4; both new modules retain 100/100/100/100. With the corrected measurement, reverting only stage/stageLocked to the unbounded implementation still fails 1/1 at 16,261,124 retained bytes. Node 26 validation is running. CI coverage gaps followed the ordinary-batch failure, which prevented the serial coverage tests from running."
  "2026-11-06T21:56:28.434Z",codex-astra,"GC-measurement correction verified: the full 13-test feature suite passes through pinned pm on both Node 22.23.4 and Node 26.13.0, without skips or cancellations. Node 22 coverage of the two new modules is 100/100/100/100. The corrected memory assertion still fails the unbounded staging-function revert at 16,261,124 bytes. Lint and test typechecking pass. Production source is byte-identical to 35f9df3, whose broader targeted suite passed 158/158. Releasing my claim after this CI test-driver fix; the item stays in_progress for orchestrator verification. Fresh exact-head CI and review receipts will be recorded on the existing PR."
  "2026-11-06T22:39:24.205Z",codex-agent,"Review round: collected all eight unresolved threads and all comments; latest CodeRabbit body has no Outside diff range section. Branch is current and contains main. Rechecking saved WIP selectively, adding behavioral revert proofs, investigating deferred-read publication atomicity and failed CI log before targeted gates."
  "2026-11-06T22:42:01.520Z",codex-agent,"Verified all seven distinct review findings. Reused correct source/link/view/test hunks from saved WIP; rejected WIP documentation-only relaxation of deferred-read guarantees. Deferred payloads now validate into private disk snapshots before any payload/provenance publication, with cleanup on refusal and success. Added real unsupported-chmod fixture. Earlier failed CI run 42276421408 failed the memory sample (11021198 bytes versus unchanged 6 MiB limit); current remote head already adds synchronous backing-store GC, which is under local verification. Current head run 42301407696 is still running, so its failed log is unavailable."
  "2026-11-06T22:46:17.391Z",codex-agent,"Self-review retained explicit-source type selection before hashing and destination view validation before writes. Added integration-level occupied-destination coverage in both merge directions, and a separate ten-file deferred-read regression checking unchanged index, object inventory, ownership namespace and derivation bytes, including cleanup after an earlier snapshot already succeeded. Existing shared all-object identity audit still rejects one non-public address; pm-vcs-identity-isolation already tracks this limitation. No history or audit policy was rewritten. Production npm audit passes with zero vulnerabilities."
  "2026-11-06T22:55:43.475Z",codex-agent,"Verified thread mapping: PRRT_kwDOToJT7M60tbr8 and PRRT_kwDOToJT7M60tbsT use no-follow source existence; PRRT_kwDOToJT7M60tbsH validates destination view; PRRT_kwDOToJT7M60tbsO and PRRT_kwDOToJT7M60tjy4 preserve explicit source link type; PRRT_kwDOToJT7M60tbsV validates all deferred snapshots before publication; PRRT_kwDOToJT7M60tbsY exercises occupied destinations through mergeTrees in both directions; PRRT_kwDOToJT7M60tbsg detects executable-permission capability and exercises unsupported chmod. First six isolated hunk/integration reverts failed the matching regressions; atomicity revert is being retried after a host-load timeout. Initial fixed feature suite passed 17/17; direct atomicity test passed 1/1. Remaining feature and focused compatibility retries use fresh memory-backed disposable trackers because disk-backed exploratory runs became resource-bound. No production thresholds changed."
  "2026-11-06T22:58:36.943Z",codex-agent,"All seven behavioral revert proofs are now confirmed in an isolated source copy: dangling inference raises ambiguous_move; dangling-copy reversion steals the source FileId; removing view validation loses the expected refusal; destination-only link typing demotes the link; reverting stageLocked to the pre-review implementation publishes nine unexpected object addresses before deferred source_changed; dropping mergeTrees conflict handoff loses the dest identity conflict; removing chmod capability detection fails on a no-op chmod filesystem. Each selected regression failed 1/1 with only its relevant production hunk/function or existing merge handoff reverted. The atomicity assertion now compares immutable addresses to avoid expensive payload failure formatting; its proof completes normally after earlier local timeout/interruption. Restored-code checks are running. No shared object or append-only history was rolled back."
  "2026-11-06T23:00:13.590Z",codex-agent,"Final implementation validation: pinned pm test --run --only-index 3 --progress --timeout 1200 passed the complete 19/19 feature suite (zero skips/cancellations); focused repository, CDC staging, composition and sparse-view compatibility passed 47/47 with the linked test command. All seven behavioral reverts failed 1/1 as recorded above; restoring every fix passed 6/6 matching cases. Node 22.23.4 passed 3/3 memory, unsupported-chmod and deferred-refusal cases with unchanged six-MiB memory allowance; the existing head GC synchronization fixes the earlier CI measurement failure. Source typecheck, build, test typecheck, lint, docstrings (101 sources, 616 declarations), zero duplication, production audit (zero vulnerabilities), package privacy (365 files, zero findings), release date and publish-attestation checks passed. Earlier resource-bound exploratory runs were interrupted or timed out; completed retries pass. Test-result persistence remains disabled by existing project policy, so receipts are recorded in comments. Full npm and Bun release gates remain assigned to PR CI at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/189/checks because this package takes several hours locally. Shared all-object identity limitation remains in the existing identity-isolation item; final committed candidate will also be checked in a fresh reachable-only clone. No new pm CLI or SDK defect was encountered."
  "2026-11-06T23:39:26.738Z",codex-agent,"Review round 2: checking new P1 PRRT_kwDOToJT7M60ukjC. The interrupted staging snapshot directory can survive SIGKILL and become foreign control storage; investigating existing recovery primitives before adding writer-lease recovery and real-process crash/erasure tests. Prior round implementation and gates are retained; no review threads will be modified."
  "2026-11-06T23:46:30.572Z",codex-agent,"P1 confirmed. Replaced named stage directories with a single descriptor registered through native objectFiles ownership. Its 0600 file name uses the already-supported empty owner-temporary class and is unlinked before the first payload write; SIGKILL closes the last descriptor automatically. No erasure allowlist expansion or deletion of unowned stage directories is needed. The initial four-case suite passed: real SIGKILL after create, after capture and after index, plus bounded positional reads/refusal of truncation. Extending the same crash cuts to shared instances and preparing function-only behavioral reverts."
  "2026-11-06T23:52:27.139Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof for PRRT_kwDOToJT7M60ukjC: in a disposable source copy, reverted only stageLocked to pushed head 3601490 (restoring its original filesystem imports). All five real SIGKILL scenarios failed at obliterate with unsupported_erasure_storage: primary creation, primary post-capture, primary post-index, shared-instance creation and shared-instance post-capture. Retrying staging did not clean the old directories. Restoring the final anonymous-snapshot implementation passed all seven new tests, including explicit-offset/truncation checks and descriptor cleanup after a deferred refusal. Children use a permissive umask; snapshot file mode remains 0600. Payload-bearing descriptors have zero links and no filename, and pre-unlink residues are empty supported owner temporaries. Namespace unlink is flushed before raw bytes are written. The whole PR diff introduces no other persistent temporary namespace."
  "2026-11-06T23:54:30.517Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 final implementation gates: pinned pm test --run --only-index 5 --progress --timeout 600 passed 7/7 new snapshot tests; --only-index 3 passed the unchanged 19/19 feature suite. Node 22.23.4 passed 8/8 crash, positional-read, descriptor-cleanup and memory-bound cases. All have zero skips/cancellations. Build, source/test typechecks, lint, docstrings (101 sources and 616 declarations), zero duplication, production dependency audit (zero vulnerabilities), package privacy (365 files and zero findings), release date and publish-attestation checks passed. No production threshold, dependency pin or erasure storage validation changed. Source diff review found only the existing supported empty owner-temporary shape; raw snapshot bytes are written only after unlink and namespace acknowledgment, and registered descriptors close on refusal/success. The existing shared-object identity audit still rejects one unrelated non-public address; the committed candidate will be checked in a fresh reachable-only clone. Full npm/Bun release certification remains delegated to PR CI at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/189/checks because local full gates take several hours. No new pm CLI/SDK bug or out-of-scope follow-up was found. Releasing this claim without closing the item; review threads are untouched."
